# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. This is a Windows project, so a checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise hand bash a script whose every line
# ends in CR, and bash reports that as `$'\r': command not found` on the very
# first line. edge/tools/create-capabilities.sh is run from Git Bash on the
# owner's machine, so this is not theoretical.
*.sh text eol=lf
